details tonight on the massive fire that  erupted yesterday at the silverstone  golf club the cause still unknown but  fire officials say this is the biggest  structural fire they have seen one of  the biggest within city limits in years  madison kimbrough joins us live near  what's left of that vacant golf club in  the northwest valley with the details  madison this isn't the first time that  golf club has caught fire right  it's not it's actually the third time  within this year that this building has  caught up in flames  when talking to firefighters many think  it may have been squatters who  previously started the flames but the  cause of the blaze that happened  yesterday is still unknown the fire  broke out around 12 30 friday afternoon  and continued to burn throughout the  night las vegas fire and rescue spent a  good seven hours before the flames were  primarily contained and due to previous  fires in this building firefighters had  to combat the flames from outside  usually in a smaller house we can get in  there we can get it under control pretty  quick get to the seat of the fire and  that's where we want to put the water  but in this particular case the building  is so big we couldn't find the seat of  the fire  and we weren't going to take a chance of  putting a firefighter in there where the  building looked like it might collapse  luckily no one was inside when the fire  started and no one was injured although  heavy smoke engulfed the neighborhood  near grand teton drive and buffalo drive  the golf club has been closed since  2015.  and there are still firefighters on  scene as you can see and zamanski said  the whole building is still a major hot  spot at this point so if you are headed  in this direction whether you live in  the neighborhood or you're on a bike  just be very very careful reporting live  in the northwest valley madison  kimbrough live local now
 

